1
00:00:13,888 --> 00:00:16,933
OUR STICKY LOVE

2
00:00:23,898 --> 00:00:25,150
Your treatment…

3
00:00:26,735 --> 00:00:27,736
Next time.

4
00:00:30,447 --> 00:00:33,199
You should have gotten it.
You went through all that trouble.

5
00:00:34,367 --> 00:00:35,493
It wasn't any trouble.

6
00:00:37,120 --> 00:00:40,080
You gave me socks
so my feet wouldn't get cold

7
00:00:40,081 --> 00:00:43,168
and loaded up the MP3 player with music
so I wouldn't get carsick.

8
00:00:44,252 --> 00:00:45,295
You did all that.

9
00:00:58,058 --> 00:01:00,684
You and your grandma…

10
00:01:00,685 --> 00:01:03,563
I know how special a bond you share.

11
00:01:05,023 --> 00:01:07,275
So I know how you must feel right now.

12
00:01:09,069 --> 00:01:12,405
Nothing is more painful
than seeing a loved one in pain.

13
00:01:16,576 --> 00:01:20,246
No matter what the results are,
there'll be a way.

14
00:01:21,998 --> 00:01:23,917
Whatever it is, I'll be here with you.

15
00:01:25,335 --> 00:01:28,171
So don't worry too much.

16
00:01:31,466 --> 00:01:32,300
Okay?

17
00:01:46,147 --> 00:01:48,524
I'm really sorry, sir.

18
00:01:48,525 --> 00:01:52,402
I didn't think
Prosecutor Go would just not show up…

19
00:01:52,403 --> 00:01:54,989
I'll do whatever it takes
to set up another meeting.

20
00:02:02,497 --> 00:02:03,832
Sir.

21
00:02:14,509 --> 00:02:15,551
Yes, that's her.

22
00:02:15,552 --> 00:02:17,219
That's Prosecutor Go.

23
00:02:17,220 --> 00:02:18,054
Yes.

24
00:02:31,985 --> 00:02:33,153
She was alive.

25
00:02:34,195 --> 00:02:35,780
This bitch was alive.

26
00:02:36,948 --> 00:02:38,575
But why has she been so quiet?

27
00:02:41,744 --> 00:02:43,538
Didn't you say it wasn't just the watch

28
00:02:44,122 --> 00:02:46,206
that could put
Mayor Ju and me behind bars?

29
00:02:46,207 --> 00:02:48,960
Yes, she definitely said that,

30
00:02:49,878 --> 00:02:52,754
but I'm not really sure
why she hasn't shown up yet.

31
00:02:52,755 --> 00:02:54,673
One thing did seem strange.

32
00:02:54,674 --> 00:02:58,010
When I was on the phone with her,
she called me Mr. Gwak Chi-hyeon.

33
00:02:58,011 --> 00:02:59,846
She's never once called me that--

34
00:03:11,733 --> 00:03:13,276
If you want to keep breathing,

35
00:03:14,569 --> 00:03:16,279
find Go Ji-won as soon as possible.

36
00:03:17,280 --> 00:03:18,114
Yes.

37
00:03:20,450 --> 00:03:22,327
I understand, sir.

38
00:03:39,594 --> 00:03:42,055
GO JI-WON 2

39
00:03:45,600 --> 00:03:47,769
This is driving me nuts.

40
00:03:51,981 --> 00:03:52,899
An ex-boyfriend?

41
00:03:53,566 --> 00:03:56,568
Okay, so in a nutshell,

42
00:03:56,569 --> 00:03:59,446
you remembered a guy
who could either be your ex

43
00:03:59,447 --> 00:04:01,573
or the guy you cheated on Tae-ha with.

44
00:04:01,574 --> 00:04:04,952
So, whether or not to tell Tae-ha

45
00:04:04,953 --> 00:04:08,830
is the critical question at hand. Correct?

46
00:04:08,831 --> 00:04:09,790
Yes.

47
00:04:09,791 --> 00:04:12,668
I don't want to keep secrets from Tae-ha,

48
00:04:12,669 --> 00:04:15,587
and it's a good thing
that I remembered something,

49
00:04:15,588 --> 00:04:17,048
so I do want to tell him.

50
00:04:18,341 --> 00:04:21,218
But it just had to be a memory of a guy.

51
00:04:21,219 --> 00:04:23,595
Goodness, I see what you're saying.

52
00:04:23,596 --> 00:04:26,640
If you ask me,
I don't think you should ever tell him.

53
00:04:26,641 --> 00:04:29,184
As a rule of thumb,
both corpses and talk of exes

54
00:04:29,185 --> 00:04:31,478
are best kept buried deep.

55
00:04:31,479 --> 00:04:33,105
- That's exactly right.
- Right.

56
00:04:33,106 --> 00:04:36,275
Surely, Tae-ha won't think
that he's your first boyfriend,

57
00:04:36,276 --> 00:04:40,446
but even if he doesn't,
actually hearing about a past guy…

58
00:04:41,030 --> 00:04:45,993
It'll start to eat away at him
like stock that's plummeted, you know?

59
00:04:45,994 --> 00:04:49,204
Just when he's about to forget,
it'll pop right into his mind.

60
00:04:49,205 --> 00:04:51,581
Or he'll get all worked up
in the dead of night.

61
00:04:51,582 --> 00:04:56,086
Or in the middle of a meal,
he'll suddenly start burning up inside!

62
00:04:56,087 --> 00:04:58,338
Did your husband dabble in stocks again?

63
00:04:58,339 --> 00:05:02,301
I'm going to stomp on that damn ape!

64
00:05:02,302 --> 00:05:04,761
Then I guess I shouldn't tell him.

65
00:05:04,762 --> 00:05:06,513
- Yeah.
- That's smart of you.

66
00:05:06,514 --> 00:05:10,893
Then let's all agree to lock this up
and throw away the key.

67
00:05:11,519 --> 00:05:12,520
Okay.

68
00:05:13,396 --> 00:05:14,355
- Please eat.
- Okay.

69
00:05:24,991 --> 00:05:26,868
I assume you didn't leave any crumbs.

70
00:05:27,744 --> 00:05:28,870
Yes, sir.

71
00:05:31,956 --> 00:05:34,000
Jang Tae-ha deceived me.

72
00:05:35,084 --> 00:05:37,253
He sure learned that from Hong Do-yeop.

73
00:05:37,837 --> 00:05:40,965
<i>I think I performed well
thanks to everything Coach Hong taught me.</i>

74
00:05:41,716 --> 00:05:46,345
<i>I'll now do my best at the Olympics
with the Taegeuk emblem on my chest.</i>

75
00:05:46,346 --> 00:05:51,476
<i>I cherish Jang Tae-ha
as if he were made from my own rib.</i>

76
00:05:52,226 --> 00:05:54,728
<i>And soon, not only me</i>

77
00:05:54,729 --> 00:05:59,901
<i>but all of Korea will come to cherish him
as a great athlete.</i>

78
00:06:08,826 --> 00:06:11,662
AN MENTAL HEALTH CLINIC

79
00:06:22,256 --> 00:06:24,342
- You're here.
- You told me to come.

80
00:06:25,176 --> 00:06:27,010
Right, I did.

81
00:06:27,011 --> 00:06:27,970
Have a seat.

82
00:06:29,180 --> 00:06:31,849
Sit down for a bit. I won't keep you long.

83
00:06:45,863 --> 00:06:46,780
What's this?

84
00:06:46,781 --> 00:06:47,949
Take a look.

85
00:06:54,956 --> 00:06:57,124
You like G-Dragon's music.

86
00:06:57,125 --> 00:06:59,127
His songs are in there.

87
00:07:00,086 --> 00:07:04,798
And it's not great
to have cold feet, so I…

88
00:07:04,799 --> 00:07:06,259
You called me to give me this?

89
00:07:07,218 --> 00:07:09,302
- What?
- Who uses MP3 players these days?

90
00:07:09,303 --> 00:07:11,097
I can afford a music subscription.

91
00:07:11,681 --> 00:07:14,434
And what's with these?
I already run hot as it is.

92
00:07:16,060 --> 00:07:18,645
Don't call me over
for stupid things like this.

93
00:07:18,646 --> 00:07:20,523
Just approve my resignation already.

94
00:07:26,279 --> 00:07:27,238
What the heck?

95
00:07:27,738 --> 00:07:32,368
Jang Tae-ha got us to turn the car around
with this. Why didn't it work for me?

96
00:07:40,251 --> 00:07:41,669
This looks delicious.

97
00:07:42,420 --> 00:07:43,463
It looks good.

98
00:07:45,631 --> 00:07:49,885
The air is so fresh. It's lovely here.

99
00:07:49,886 --> 00:07:52,804
How are you feeling, ma'am?
Are you feeling better?

100
00:07:52,805 --> 00:07:55,892
Well, it reminds me of the war. It's nice.

101
00:07:58,436 --> 00:07:59,686
Should we go elsewhere?

102
00:07:59,687 --> 00:08:03,648
It took you over an hour
to set up that tent.

103
00:08:03,649 --> 00:08:05,401
It'd be a waste. Let's just stay.

104
00:08:06,068 --> 00:08:06,903
Sure.

105
00:08:08,863 --> 00:08:11,449
- I'll go buy a new one. Is it out of gas?
- No, I'll go.

106
00:08:12,366 --> 00:08:14,911
Hurry up and get things ready.
She's hungry.

107
00:08:25,880 --> 00:08:27,214
Goodness.

108
00:08:27,215 --> 00:08:30,760
We should be grilling meat
at a place like this.

109
00:08:31,260 --> 00:08:34,554
You can't have grilled meat.
Don't you know what condition you're in?

110
00:08:34,555 --> 00:08:37,432
How much longer
do you think I have to live?

111
00:08:37,433 --> 00:08:38,350
Grandma.

112
00:08:38,351 --> 00:08:42,104
Why would you even
say something like that?

113
00:08:43,940 --> 00:08:47,443
So don't spend money on my treatment.

114
00:08:48,444 --> 00:08:49,737
- Okay?
- No.

115
00:08:50,947 --> 00:08:54,158
I'll save you no matter what.

116
00:08:54,659 --> 00:08:58,871
You've been saving me my whole life.
What more is there to save?

117
00:09:00,498 --> 00:09:04,626
I lost your mom to an illness
just when I was getting attached.

118
00:09:04,627 --> 00:09:06,003
Just my luck.

119
00:09:07,046 --> 00:09:09,548
I wouldn't have missed a thing
even if I died back then.

120
00:09:09,549 --> 00:09:12,385
A truly miserable life.

121
00:09:13,302 --> 00:09:16,097
But you breathed life into me.

122
00:09:17,181 --> 00:09:23,354
Even when life threw me
mountains upon mountains of sorrow,

123
00:09:24,522 --> 00:09:27,567
I gritted my teeth and lived on
because of you.

124
00:09:28,276 --> 00:09:31,278
So it's enough now.

125
00:09:31,279 --> 00:09:34,240
It's time you stopped saving me.

126
00:09:36,450 --> 00:09:38,910
For the rest of my days,

127
00:09:38,911 --> 00:09:42,790
instead of reeling in pain
from that excruciating treatment,

128
00:09:43,666 --> 00:09:47,461
and instead of staring at the faces
of doctors I don't even know,

129
00:09:48,254 --> 00:09:53,634
I want to go back to making taffy,
the thing that kept food on the table.

130
00:09:55,386 --> 00:09:56,721
You, my precious baby.

131
00:09:57,722 --> 00:09:59,807
My pitiful Song-wol.

132
00:10:00,308 --> 00:10:04,312
And the villagers who are kind-hearted
once you get to know them.

133
00:10:05,104 --> 00:10:06,147
All of you.

134
00:10:07,231 --> 00:10:11,235
I want to spend my last days
taking you all in.

135
00:10:13,654 --> 00:10:14,905
Tae-ha.

136
00:10:15,906 --> 00:10:20,036
Please let me do that, okay?

137
00:10:22,330 --> 00:10:23,831
Don't cry.

138
00:10:24,332 --> 00:10:28,961
It breaks my heart to see
that handsome face of yours downcast.

139
00:10:34,675 --> 00:10:35,885
By the way,

140
00:10:36,761 --> 00:10:41,307
are you thinking of marrying that girl?

141
00:10:44,602 --> 00:10:48,188
My whole body aches
from walking around all day.

142
00:10:48,189 --> 00:10:49,231
Goodness.

143
00:10:52,109 --> 00:10:53,485
I'm back.

144
00:10:53,486 --> 00:10:55,196
Oh, you're back?

145
00:10:55,863 --> 00:10:56,906
Ma'am.

146
00:11:01,786 --> 00:11:02,952
Gang-rok,

147
00:11:02,953 --> 00:11:04,621
you got your cast off?

148
00:11:04,622 --> 00:11:09,042
Yes. I know I don't look like it,
but I <i>am</i> in my twenties.

149
00:11:09,043 --> 00:11:10,503
They said I heal super quickly.

150
00:11:12,338 --> 00:11:13,672
That's great.

151
00:11:13,673 --> 00:11:16,550
Right? Now that my foot's back,

152
00:11:17,051 --> 00:11:20,178
you can ask me to run errands
as much as you want.

153
00:11:20,179 --> 00:11:22,555
- Really? Can I do that?
- Of course.

154
00:11:22,556 --> 00:11:24,933
Really? Then can you find me something?

155
00:11:24,934 --> 00:11:27,019
Yes, ma'am! What shall I procure for you?

156
00:11:27,728 --> 00:11:29,230
A house for you.

157
00:11:32,775 --> 00:11:36,779
I'd understand if you had lived abroad.

158
00:11:37,405 --> 00:11:40,115
Because there's no specific term
for "reading social cues."

159
00:11:40,116 --> 00:11:42,575
But you were born and raised in Korea.

160
00:11:42,576 --> 00:11:45,537
How long do I have to let you have my man?

161
00:11:45,538 --> 00:11:48,833
I told him to go to your room,
but he was the one who refused.

162
00:11:50,501 --> 00:11:51,793
Then what should you do?

163
00:11:51,794 --> 00:11:55,130
Either shove him into my room by force

164
00:11:55,131 --> 00:11:57,507
or hurry to find a house and move out.

165
00:11:57,508 --> 00:11:58,842
I already found one.

166
00:11:58,843 --> 00:12:00,218
Wait, you did?

167
00:12:00,219 --> 00:12:01,429
I'm moving out tomorrow.

168
00:12:03,264 --> 00:12:04,265
Tomorrow?

169
00:12:04,765 --> 00:12:07,350
Why didn't you say so?

170
00:12:07,351 --> 00:12:09,936
What a shame. Where are you going?

171
00:12:09,937 --> 00:12:11,771
It's a five-minute walk from here.

172
00:12:11,772 --> 00:12:14,066
A five-minute walk? I see.

173
00:12:15,276 --> 00:12:17,736
I'm so sad. What should we do?

174
00:12:17,737 --> 00:12:19,739
Should we have a farewell party?

175
00:12:20,823 --> 00:12:22,282
No need for a farewell party.

176
00:12:22,283 --> 00:12:25,786
Why don't we have some banquet noodles?
Since you seem so keen to celebrate.

177
00:12:26,996 --> 00:12:29,123
Banquet noodles sound perfect.

178
00:12:30,416 --> 00:12:31,459
I'm fine.

179
00:12:32,126 --> 00:12:33,377
You should go now.

180
00:12:33,878 --> 00:12:37,131
Thanks to you, I had a great time today.

181
00:12:37,715 --> 00:12:39,175
I'll sleep well tonight.

182
00:12:40,551 --> 00:12:41,594
That's good to hear.

183
00:12:43,137 --> 00:12:46,098
About what I mentioned earlier.

184
00:12:47,641 --> 00:12:48,893
Your marriage.

185
00:12:51,937 --> 00:12:54,606
What I wanted to say about
your marriage was…

186
00:12:54,607 --> 00:12:55,523
Marriage?

187
00:12:55,524 --> 00:12:56,859
I know what you want to say.

188
00:12:57,777 --> 00:12:59,068
Don't worry about it.

189
00:12:59,069 --> 00:12:59,945
Good night.

190
00:13:00,571 --> 00:13:01,405
You too.

191
00:13:12,041 --> 00:13:12,875
Let's go home.

192
00:13:14,418 --> 00:13:15,544
- Okay.
- Okay.

193
00:13:20,424 --> 00:13:22,551
I want to respect her wishes,

194
00:13:23,052 --> 00:13:25,721
so from now on, I'll do my best
to give her happy memories.

195
00:13:28,849 --> 00:13:29,683
Thanks.

196
00:13:31,936 --> 00:13:33,646
For making today great for her.

197
00:13:36,690 --> 00:13:39,192
By the way,
what were you two talking about earlier?

198
00:13:39,193 --> 00:13:40,027
What?

199
00:13:40,986 --> 00:13:45,282
I heard something about marriage.
Does she want us to get married soon?

200
00:13:47,868 --> 00:13:48,702
It's nothing.

201
00:13:51,831 --> 00:13:52,998
Okay.

202
00:13:53,916 --> 00:13:55,000
Marriage?

203
00:13:55,501 --> 00:13:57,752
I guess they're setting a date soon.

204
00:13:57,753 --> 00:13:59,129
How wonderful!

205
00:14:07,388 --> 00:14:11,057
Fine, I'll act clueless.

206
00:14:11,058 --> 00:14:14,018
What else could she have said,
bringing up marriage?

207
00:14:14,019 --> 00:14:15,938
She must have told him
to rush the wedding.

208
00:14:17,231 --> 00:14:19,149
Why is he hiding that from me?

209
00:14:20,943 --> 00:14:22,402
Is he planning to propose?

210
00:14:22,403 --> 00:14:26,198
Should I give him a hint
that a small, pretty bouquet will do?

211
00:14:27,157 --> 00:14:29,951
Wait, so I'm actually getting married?

212
00:14:29,952 --> 00:14:32,746
Oh my God, I'm so happy!

213
00:14:35,332 --> 00:14:36,667
Roses?

214
00:14:37,793 --> 00:14:38,710
Yeah.

215
00:14:38,711 --> 00:14:40,795
All women like roses.

216
00:14:40,796 --> 00:14:44,550
Your grandma loved the flowers yesterday.
You should give her flowers more often.

217
00:14:45,134 --> 00:14:47,928
Baby pink roses are so pretty.

218
00:14:49,054 --> 00:14:50,055
Sure.

219
00:14:50,681 --> 00:14:53,934
She's asking you to buy her flowers
in a roundabout way.

220
00:15:01,525 --> 00:15:02,359
Goodness.

221
00:15:02,860 --> 00:15:06,237
Where are you going with that shovel?

222
00:15:06,238 --> 00:15:09,241
Gang-rok's moving out today,
so I'm helping tidy up his yard.

223
00:15:09,825 --> 00:15:10,784
I see.

224
00:15:11,285 --> 00:15:15,080
So, the soon-to-be bride and groom
will finally be living alone again.

225
00:15:15,873 --> 00:15:17,123
Yes.

226
00:15:17,124 --> 00:15:21,170
Maeng-suk said she heard yesterday
that you two are planning the wedding.

227
00:15:21,754 --> 00:15:23,838
You better tell us the date in advance.

228
00:15:23,839 --> 00:15:25,883
We're all busy people, you know.

229
00:15:27,259 --> 00:15:28,468
That won't happen.

230
00:15:28,469 --> 00:15:29,386
What?

231
00:15:31,555 --> 00:15:32,806
You're not getting married?

232
00:15:34,850 --> 00:15:36,435
We're not. Well, then…

233
00:15:41,774 --> 00:15:42,608
What the…

234
00:15:43,192 --> 00:15:46,820
Maeng-suk said
she clearly heard them yesterday.

235
00:15:51,909 --> 00:15:53,284
I just told you.

236
00:15:53,285 --> 00:15:54,702
- Right.
- But…

237
00:15:54,703 --> 00:15:56,205
- Yes?
- Hui-ja.

238
00:15:56,997 --> 00:15:58,831
The heck's going on?

239
00:15:58,832 --> 00:16:00,041
What is it?

240
00:16:00,042 --> 00:16:01,834
It's about Tae-ha.

241
00:16:01,835 --> 00:16:04,963
I just met him,
and he said he's not getting married.

242
00:16:04,964 --> 00:16:05,923
What?

243
00:16:07,675 --> 00:16:11,094
We were actually just talking about that.

244
00:16:11,095 --> 00:16:11,929
You were?

245
00:16:12,513 --> 00:16:13,973
The thing is,

246
00:16:14,556 --> 00:16:18,352
I went to Tae-ha's to give him
some boiled pork this morning.

247
00:16:19,895 --> 00:16:22,272
I'm not keeping her around
because I want to.

248
00:16:22,773 --> 00:16:26,151
You know I'm not too fond of them.

249
00:16:27,111 --> 00:16:27,945
But what can I do?

250
00:16:28,612 --> 00:16:31,906
She has nowhere to go and no family.

251
00:16:31,907 --> 00:16:32,741
I feel bad.

252
00:16:33,701 --> 00:16:35,536
I'm just used to having her around now.

253
00:16:38,580 --> 00:16:40,207
Wait. One second.

254
00:16:41,625 --> 00:16:42,918
Hey.

255
00:16:45,671 --> 00:16:47,672
Well, see,

256
00:16:47,673 --> 00:16:50,299
I made some boiled pork
early this morning.

257
00:16:50,300 --> 00:16:52,886
It's good, so I thought I'd…
Do you want to try it?

258
00:16:53,804 --> 00:16:55,346
- Thank you.
- Sure.

259
00:16:55,347 --> 00:16:57,016
- I'll enjoy it.
- Okay.

260
00:16:58,058 --> 00:16:59,600
Go on with what you were doing.

261
00:16:59,601 --> 00:17:00,686
I'll be going.

262
00:17:12,865 --> 00:17:15,951
Now she runs to me whenever she sees me
and doesn't even bark.

263
00:17:16,702 --> 00:17:17,786
She's ours now.

264
00:17:18,829 --> 00:17:22,875
Then I'll bring you some dog food later.

265
00:17:23,459 --> 00:17:24,334
Okay.

266
00:17:26,295 --> 00:17:27,211
Good heavens.

267
00:17:27,212 --> 00:17:30,006
Did he really say he took her in
because he felt bad for her,

268
00:17:30,007 --> 00:17:31,841
even though he has no feelings for her?

269
00:17:31,842 --> 00:17:35,261
That's what he said.
I heard it clearly with my own ears.

270
00:17:35,262 --> 00:17:38,682
He went around acting like
Taffy Village's biggest hopeless romantic.

271
00:17:39,266 --> 00:17:41,142
Do you really think Tae-ha would…

272
00:17:41,143 --> 00:17:44,396
- Come on, no way!
- Come on, no way!

273
00:17:52,571 --> 00:17:55,698
I wanted to set the mood
after Gang-rok left,

274
00:17:55,699 --> 00:17:58,744
but all my pajamas are frumpy.

275
00:17:59,995 --> 00:18:02,164
BOOST YOUR CURVES AND YOUR CONFIDENCE
PUSH-UP PADS

276
00:18:04,374 --> 00:18:05,542
Well, well.

277
00:18:29,108 --> 00:18:31,276
Hello.

278
00:18:32,820 --> 00:18:34,613
Is Tae-ha not around today?

279
00:18:37,116 --> 00:18:38,699
Why do you ask about my man?

280
00:18:38,700 --> 00:18:40,661
You're always together.

281
00:18:41,161 --> 00:18:43,205
I didn't know he was that sweet.

282
00:18:44,665 --> 00:18:47,209
Well, what was he like in school?

283
00:18:48,085 --> 00:18:49,670
Doesn't he tell you about himself?

284
00:18:51,004 --> 00:18:51,839
I'm sure he did.

285
00:18:52,673 --> 00:18:55,425
I'm sure he told me lots.
I just don't remember.

286
00:18:55,926 --> 00:18:59,847
Right, since you don't have your memory,
you must not know much about Tae-ha.

287
00:19:00,681 --> 00:19:04,143
In a way, you must not be that close,
even though he's your boyfriend.

288
00:19:09,273 --> 00:19:12,693
And were you close with him?

289
00:19:13,360 --> 00:19:14,194
Why do you ask?

290
00:19:16,238 --> 00:19:18,282
We're getting married soon, you see.

291
00:19:18,782 --> 00:19:21,410
I was wondering
if I should give you an invitation.

292
00:19:26,498 --> 00:19:28,500
Give me one. I'll be there.

293
00:19:30,294 --> 00:19:31,461
Congratulations.

294
00:19:32,713 --> 00:19:33,547
Thanks.

295
00:19:45,350 --> 00:19:49,188
What is this? Why do I feel sorry for her
all of a sudden?

296
00:19:50,272 --> 00:19:51,355
- Gang-rok.
- Yes?

297
00:19:51,356 --> 00:19:52,273
Take it easy.

298
00:19:52,274 --> 00:19:53,275
Yes, sir.

299
00:19:55,736 --> 00:19:59,071
Sir, I have a question.

300
00:19:59,072 --> 00:20:02,868
Remember the lady that Ms. Go asked me
to take home last time?

301
00:20:03,660 --> 00:20:04,828
What?

302
00:20:07,664 --> 00:20:08,665
Su-ji?

303
00:20:09,458 --> 00:20:10,292
Su-ji…

304
00:20:11,585 --> 00:20:14,463
How do you know her exactly?

305
00:20:15,047 --> 00:20:15,881
A classmate.

306
00:20:17,132 --> 00:20:17,966
A classmate.

307
00:20:18,550 --> 00:20:20,968
She's so pretty.

308
00:20:20,969 --> 00:20:23,304
I keep thinking about her.

309
00:20:23,305 --> 00:20:27,559
So I was wondering if there was
someone on her mind.

310
00:20:29,728 --> 00:20:32,439
I'm not sure.
I don't really know her that well.

311
00:20:34,274 --> 00:20:37,985
Back in your passionate teenage years,
you had a beauty like her as a classmate,

312
00:20:37,986 --> 00:20:39,780
and you didn't feel anything?

313
00:20:44,284 --> 00:20:46,078
How could you even do that?

314
00:20:46,954 --> 00:20:49,164
I don't know.
I've never seen her that way.

315
00:20:50,707 --> 00:20:53,293
- <i>I've never seen her that way</i>.
- Doesn't see her that way?

316
00:20:59,341 --> 00:21:02,844
Then again, you've been devoted
solely to Ms. Go your whole life.

317
00:21:07,474 --> 00:21:10,686
Are you sure
you'll be able to send her away?

318
00:21:19,403 --> 00:21:20,279
I'll send her away

319
00:21:20,862 --> 00:21:22,155
once her memory returns.

320
00:21:23,949 --> 00:21:24,950
I can do it.

321
00:21:26,285 --> 00:21:27,286
I can let her go.

322
00:21:46,346 --> 00:21:49,890
So he's saying he'll send her away
as soon as she gets her memory back,

323
00:21:49,891 --> 00:21:53,102
but since she hasn't,
he's just keeping her around for now?

324
00:21:53,103 --> 00:21:56,898
She has no memory and no family,
so he pities her?

325
00:21:59,109 --> 00:22:01,110
That little rascal!

326
00:22:01,111 --> 00:22:02,988
Tae-ha's just like the rest of them!

327
00:22:03,572 --> 00:22:07,575
If he felt that way, he shouldn't have
doted on her so much.

328
00:22:07,576 --> 00:22:09,161
Damn it!

329
00:22:09,661 --> 00:22:11,454
Why, I ought to just…

330
00:22:11,455 --> 00:22:13,123
Ladies!

331
00:22:15,584 --> 00:22:17,002
I'm here.

332
00:22:23,884 --> 00:22:24,926
Oh no.

333
00:22:26,511 --> 00:22:27,971
Well, this is…

334
00:22:31,683 --> 00:22:33,018
With this,

335
00:22:33,560 --> 00:22:35,020
you could survive a gunshot.

336
00:22:36,938 --> 00:22:40,399
It's just that Gang-rok moved out today.

337
00:22:40,400 --> 00:22:44,571
Since it'll just be the two of us at home,
I've been doing some preparing.

338
00:22:45,155 --> 00:22:47,657
I want to show him a new side of myself.

339
00:22:49,076 --> 00:22:51,161
Come on, you know what I'm talking about.

340
00:22:53,872 --> 00:22:55,374
I can't bear to watch.

341
00:22:56,541 --> 00:23:00,170
I can't do it.
I just want to tell her everything.

342
00:23:03,340 --> 00:23:05,257
- Okay, I'm coming.
- That way.

343
00:23:05,258 --> 00:23:06,634
- Hurry.
- Okay!

344
00:23:06,635 --> 00:23:09,596
- Sit.
- Sit here.

345
00:23:13,100 --> 00:23:16,685
So, what we're saying is,
Tae-ha has no intention of marrying you,

346
00:23:16,686 --> 00:23:19,814
so don't smile at him like that
or give him everything.

347
00:23:19,815 --> 00:23:21,274
Have some pride!

348
00:23:22,025 --> 00:23:24,235
He doesn't even see you that way.

349
00:23:24,236 --> 00:23:27,238
Stuffing your chest
like a prize-winning turkey for him

350
00:23:27,239 --> 00:23:29,031
will only make you look ridiculous!

351
00:23:29,032 --> 00:23:32,827
What kind of nonsense
are you all talking about?

352
00:23:32,828 --> 00:23:36,248
You have no idea how much he likes me.

353
00:23:36,748 --> 00:23:39,875
He's only being nice to you
because he feels bad for you, okay?

354
00:23:39,876 --> 00:23:42,671
Because you have no memory
and nowhere else to go.

355
00:23:43,296 --> 00:23:47,967
- Like taking in a stray dog.
- Goodness gracious. Stop it.

356
00:23:47,968 --> 00:23:50,052
This is just breaking my heart.

357
00:23:50,053 --> 00:23:54,807
I can't stand to see our dear Eun-sae
look like a complete fool.

358
00:23:54,808 --> 00:23:59,563
I don't know
what it is you all heard or saw,

359
00:24:00,147 --> 00:24:02,731
but it's all a misunderstanding!

360
00:24:02,732 --> 00:24:05,485
Jang Tae-ha is crazy about me.

361
00:24:07,320 --> 00:24:08,738
So don't worry about me.

362
00:24:10,532 --> 00:24:12,450
We're going to set the date soon,

363
00:24:12,451 --> 00:24:14,661
so come over
and have some banquet noodles.

364
00:24:15,245 --> 00:24:16,079
Well, then,

365
00:24:17,205 --> 00:24:19,249
I'll get going.

366
00:24:19,833 --> 00:24:21,168
Tonight's pretty important.

367
00:24:26,173 --> 00:24:28,924
Don't run. The pads will fall out!

368
00:24:28,925 --> 00:24:31,093
- What do we do?
- What should we do with her?

369
00:24:31,094 --> 00:24:32,553
I feel so bad for her.

370
00:24:32,554 --> 00:24:34,263
What do we do?

371
00:24:34,264 --> 00:24:35,891
- This is insane.
- What to do?

372
00:24:45,692 --> 00:24:48,236
Those ladies are ridiculous.

373
00:24:48,737 --> 00:24:53,116
How could they misunderstand
Jang Tae-ha of all people?

374
00:25:11,259 --> 00:25:12,594
You're home.

375
00:25:16,848 --> 00:25:17,849
Yeah.

376
00:25:47,045 --> 00:25:48,755
I've been waiting for you.

377
00:25:51,383 --> 00:25:52,384
Why?

378
00:25:55,762 --> 00:25:57,347
What do you mean "why"?

379
00:25:58,056 --> 00:26:00,517
Now that Gang-rok has moved out,

380
00:26:01,226 --> 00:26:03,186
we have a lot to do.

381
00:26:04,854 --> 00:26:08,232
We don't have to sleep
in separate rooms anymore,

382
00:26:08,233 --> 00:26:10,860
so we should clean up a bit.

383
00:26:11,361 --> 00:26:13,571
We can use my room as our bedroom.

384
00:26:13,572 --> 00:26:14,739
Right, well…

385
00:26:17,117 --> 00:26:18,577
Some other time.

386
00:26:19,160 --> 00:26:20,662
I'm…

387
00:26:21,162 --> 00:26:23,331
a bit tired today.

388
00:26:24,499 --> 00:26:25,458
So…

389
00:26:26,835 --> 00:26:28,503
cleaning will be a little…

390
00:26:33,174 --> 00:26:34,009
No…

391
00:26:36,595 --> 00:26:37,721
I mean…

392
00:26:39,723 --> 00:26:42,183
that's not the only thing
I was talking about.

393
00:26:48,982 --> 00:26:51,526
Wait, where did the dog go?

394
00:26:53,612 --> 00:26:56,615
Our dog isn't in the yard.

395
00:26:57,324 --> 00:27:00,952
I'll go find her right away.

396
00:27:04,664 --> 00:27:06,291
I'll be right back.

397
00:27:13,214 --> 00:27:14,049
The dog?

398
00:27:19,346 --> 00:27:21,014
She's just going to…

399
00:27:21,598 --> 00:27:23,266
If she comes on hard like that, I…

400
00:27:32,400 --> 00:27:36,363
Does someone who's tired
run out like that to find a dog?

401
00:27:38,865 --> 00:27:41,034
He's definitely dodging me on purpose.

402
00:27:41,618 --> 00:27:43,161
But why?

403
00:27:46,039 --> 00:27:48,207
<i>He doesn't even see you that way.</i>

404
00:27:48,208 --> 00:27:51,168
<i>Stuffing your chest
like a prize-winning turkey for him</i>

405
00:27:51,169 --> 00:27:53,004
<i>will only make you look ridiculous!</i>

406
00:27:58,343 --> 00:27:59,427
No, it can't be.

407
00:28:00,470 --> 00:28:01,721
That's impossible.

408
00:28:02,514 --> 00:28:04,516
I liked you from the moment I saw you.

409
00:28:13,525 --> 00:28:14,943
Yeah.

410
00:28:15,860 --> 00:28:18,530
His eyes weren't lying.

411
00:28:20,490 --> 00:28:21,990
Silly me.

412
00:28:21,991 --> 00:28:25,370
What am I thinking? Dummy.

413
00:28:36,798 --> 00:28:38,299
Don't disappear on me again.

414
00:28:40,009 --> 00:28:41,928
Just don't disappear without a word.

415
00:28:44,139 --> 00:28:46,098
<i>He's only being nice because he feels bad.</i>

416
00:28:46,099 --> 00:28:48,268
<i>Like taking in a stray dog.</i>

417
00:28:53,481 --> 00:28:54,733
This won't do.

418
00:29:05,118 --> 00:29:07,077
Good thing I went looking for her.

419
00:29:07,078 --> 00:29:09,789
She was stuck in a ditch on a farm.

420
00:29:12,000 --> 00:29:13,585
That was a close call.

421
00:29:14,961 --> 00:29:16,504
Won't we sleep together tonight?

422
00:29:17,714 --> 00:29:19,382
- What?
- Answer me.

423
00:29:19,966 --> 00:29:20,884
Right…

424
00:29:21,551 --> 00:29:22,927
Well…

425
00:29:24,137 --> 00:29:25,805
I'm a bit

426
00:29:26,306 --> 00:29:27,140
tired today.

427
00:29:29,017 --> 00:29:31,143
<i>Tae-ha has no intention of marrying you,</i>

428
00:29:31,144 --> 00:29:34,689
<i>so don't smile at him like that
or give him everything.</i>

429
00:29:37,484 --> 00:29:38,735
What about our marriage?

430
00:29:40,570 --> 00:29:42,071
Is that not

431
00:29:42,947 --> 00:29:43,782
happening?

432
00:29:47,535 --> 00:29:48,536
About that…

433
00:29:52,123 --> 00:29:53,708
Let's talk about that…

434
00:29:55,210 --> 00:29:56,502
after you regain your memory.

435
00:29:56,503 --> 00:29:57,461
Why?

436
00:29:57,462 --> 00:29:59,671
You haven't gotten
your memory back yet, and--

437
00:29:59,672 --> 00:30:02,633
What does that have to do with
getting my memory back?

438
00:30:02,634 --> 00:30:05,762
You said we were planning on
getting married!

439
00:30:06,471 --> 00:30:07,430
Still,

440
00:30:08,389 --> 00:30:09,724
getting your memory back

441
00:30:11,017 --> 00:30:12,060
comes first.

442
00:30:25,490 --> 00:30:28,408
You should've told me

443
00:30:28,409 --> 00:30:32,705
that you were living with me
because you felt bad for me.

444
00:30:36,042 --> 00:30:39,545
You were so nice to me

445
00:30:39,546 --> 00:30:41,714
when you never even saw me that way.

446
00:30:42,215 --> 00:30:46,469
And you even kissed me, damn you!

447
00:30:49,597 --> 00:30:51,391
Why did you do that?

448
00:30:51,975 --> 00:30:52,976
Why?

449
00:31:07,031 --> 00:31:08,199
Are you going somewhere?

450
00:31:11,619 --> 00:31:13,787
I'm going to meet the S.E.S ladies.

451
00:31:13,788 --> 00:31:14,956
Now?

452
00:31:17,208 --> 00:31:18,376
I'll walk you.

453
00:31:19,919 --> 00:31:20,919
It's fine.

454
00:31:20,920 --> 00:31:23,131
I'm not like the dog,

455
00:31:23,631 --> 00:31:25,675
so I can find my way home just fine.

456
00:31:39,564 --> 00:31:41,065
She seems mad.

457
00:31:57,916 --> 00:31:59,750
We're getting married soon, you see.

458
00:31:59,751 --> 00:32:02,795
I was wondering
if I should give you an invitation.

459
00:32:13,598 --> 00:32:15,558
What are you doing here?

460
00:32:19,062 --> 00:32:20,396
Min Su-ji.

461
00:32:22,732 --> 00:32:26,151
How long are you going to keep this up?
Just work at the clinic.

462
00:32:26,152 --> 00:32:29,237
And you can just keep dating me.
What's the problem?

463
00:32:29,238 --> 00:32:30,781
Do you really not know?

464
00:32:30,782 --> 00:32:31,740
I don't.

465
00:32:31,741 --> 00:32:33,241
I have no idea.

466
00:32:33,242 --> 00:32:35,744
I don't see why you're making
a huge deal out of this.

467
00:32:35,745 --> 00:32:38,789
And I don't know what I have to do
to make you feel better.

468
00:32:38,790 --> 00:32:42,459
Go Eun-sae was moved to tears
when Jang Tae-ha gave her a pair of socks,

469
00:32:42,460 --> 00:32:45,672
but I have no clue what to do
to make you feel satisfied.

470
00:32:50,093 --> 00:32:50,927
What?

471
00:32:51,844 --> 00:32:52,929
What is it?

472
00:32:54,764 --> 00:32:57,558
Tae-ha and Ms. Go are getting married.

473
00:32:58,685 --> 00:32:59,601
They are?

474
00:32:59,602 --> 00:33:03,606
Why do you think she's marrying Tae-ha
when she doesn't even remember him?

475
00:33:04,357 --> 00:33:05,942
Jang Tae-ha is sincere.

476
00:33:07,068 --> 00:33:08,695
Do you even know how to be sincere?

477
00:33:10,196 --> 00:33:11,030
Why wouldn't I?

478
00:33:11,864 --> 00:33:13,992
Hey, I'm sincere too. Toward you.

479
00:33:16,119 --> 00:33:17,912
Sincerity isn't spoken.

480
00:33:18,621 --> 00:33:20,039
You can see it.

481
00:33:23,001 --> 00:33:24,877
Let's stop this, An Gi-jun.

482
00:33:30,550 --> 00:33:32,260
Oh, come on.

483
00:33:33,386 --> 00:33:34,928
Come on!

484
00:33:34,929 --> 00:33:36,139
Damn it.

485
00:33:39,892 --> 00:33:43,061
Why is Go Eun-sae getting married
without even checking the facts?

486
00:33:43,062 --> 00:33:43,896
Is she crazy?

487
00:33:46,691 --> 00:33:48,609
Hello, Ms. Go. Are you and Tae-ha really…

488
00:33:49,610 --> 00:33:50,486
Hello?

489
00:33:51,612 --> 00:33:53,448
What the heck's up with her?

490
00:34:04,459 --> 00:34:06,461
- You're here.
- What's going on?

491
00:34:07,962 --> 00:34:09,422
You had four bottles alone?

492
00:34:10,131 --> 00:34:12,050
They just sort of piled up.

493
00:34:13,217 --> 00:34:14,801
- All this?
- Need an extra glass?

494
00:34:14,802 --> 00:34:16,011
No, I'm good.

495
00:34:16,012 --> 00:34:17,013
Hey.

496
00:34:17,889 --> 00:34:19,807
I heard you're marrying Tae-ha.

497
00:34:20,349 --> 00:34:23,227
Are you sure you won't regret it?
Are you not going to Seoul?

498
00:34:25,730 --> 00:34:27,273
Married?

499
00:34:32,361 --> 00:34:34,404
The thing is, Doctor,

500
00:34:34,405 --> 00:34:36,866
I like Jang Tae-ha.

501
00:34:37,909 --> 00:34:42,038
I really, truly like him.

502
00:34:43,831 --> 00:34:44,748
So what?

503
00:34:44,749 --> 00:34:47,668
He shouldn't have made me fall for him.

504
00:34:48,169 --> 00:34:51,671
What am I supposed to do
if he makes me like him this much

505
00:34:51,672 --> 00:34:54,926
and then goes and does that?

506
00:34:55,510 --> 00:34:57,470
What am I supposed to do?

507
00:35:01,808 --> 00:35:04,268
And what am <i>I</i> supposed to do?
I'm calling Jang Tae-ha.

508
00:35:05,061 --> 00:35:06,687
- No, please.
- You drank too much.

509
00:35:07,188 --> 00:35:09,064
- Don't.
- Why not?

510
00:35:09,065 --> 00:35:13,319
He'll hate me even more
if he sees me like this.

511
00:35:13,903 --> 00:35:15,696
Don't you dare call him.

512
00:35:19,117 --> 00:35:20,409
Give me that.

513
00:35:20,993 --> 00:35:23,996
Wait, don't put that in there…

514
00:35:24,705 --> 00:35:25,832
Seriously?

515
00:35:27,291 --> 00:35:30,628
Why is everyone…
What do you expect me to do?

516
00:35:53,025 --> 00:35:55,403
What's taking her so long?

517
00:36:06,914 --> 00:36:08,166
Here.

518
00:36:12,211 --> 00:36:13,128
Almost there.

519
00:36:13,129 --> 00:36:14,755
What on earth happened?

520
00:36:15,673 --> 00:36:18,134
- She said she was meeting the ladies.
- Take her.

521
00:36:20,553 --> 00:36:21,512
Careful.

522
00:36:26,517 --> 00:36:28,019
She was drinking alone.

523
00:36:28,728 --> 00:36:30,770
Alone? Why would she…

524
00:36:30,771 --> 00:36:33,106
She wouldn't let me call
in case it bothered you.

525
00:36:33,107 --> 00:36:34,859
And she has my phone.

526
00:36:35,985 --> 00:36:37,028
In her back pocket.

527
00:36:44,744 --> 00:36:45,661
Well,

528
00:36:46,370 --> 00:36:47,330
since I'm here,

529
00:36:47,830 --> 00:36:50,208
let me ask you straight out.

530
00:36:51,209 --> 00:36:53,377
Are you really her boyfriend?

531
00:36:54,712 --> 00:36:58,049
If you set out to, it'd be easy
to trick someone who has no memory.

532
00:36:58,633 --> 00:37:01,969
You were a gangster,
so I bet it wouldn't be beneath you.

533
00:37:03,346 --> 00:37:07,098
Why does Ms. Go trust you so much
when she remembers nothing?

534
00:37:07,099 --> 00:37:09,059
How did you get her

535
00:37:09,060 --> 00:37:11,353
so taken with you
without a shred of proof?

536
00:37:11,354 --> 00:37:12,480
Not just her, everyone!

537
00:37:22,740 --> 00:37:25,076
I appreciate you bringing her here,

538
00:37:26,619 --> 00:37:28,204
but watch what you say.

539
00:37:38,839 --> 00:37:39,757
Let's go.

540
00:37:47,098 --> 00:37:48,890
<i>Jang Tae-ha is sincere.</i>

541
00:37:48,891 --> 00:37:50,935
<i>Jang Tae-ha is real.</i>

542
00:37:52,103 --> 00:37:53,062
And if it's all fake?

543
00:37:56,357 --> 00:37:57,984
What will you do if it's all a lie?

544
00:38:12,290 --> 00:38:13,124
Yes?

545
00:38:14,583 --> 00:38:17,168
- You're who?
- Someone who knows Ms. Go Ji-won well.

546
00:38:17,169 --> 00:38:18,379
Ji-won?

547
00:38:19,255 --> 00:38:20,922
Where is she right now?

548
00:38:20,923 --> 00:38:23,426
I'm actually hoping to meet you
regarding that matter.

549
00:38:24,010 --> 00:38:26,679
Could you spare me some time?

550
00:38:31,684 --> 00:38:33,269
Was it around ten years ago?

551
00:38:33,769 --> 00:38:36,647
When we took over
the Hijikata faction in Osaka,

552
00:38:37,273 --> 00:38:41,110
their chairman gifted me this guy,
along with a warning.

553
00:38:42,403 --> 00:38:47,241
"Arowanas still have the instinct to jump
from when they hunted in the wild,

554
00:38:48,367 --> 00:38:50,286
so make sure
to cover the top of the tank."

555
00:38:50,995 --> 00:38:54,665
He warned that the moment I opened the lid

556
00:38:55,499 --> 00:38:57,918
to give him some air…

557
00:39:07,136 --> 00:39:09,220
he'd splash water like this.

558
00:39:09,221 --> 00:39:10,930
<i>He'll be a great athlete.</i>

559
00:39:10,931 --> 00:39:13,100
GOLD MEDAL HOPEFUL JANG TAE-HA
WINS NATIONAL TEAM TRIALS

560
00:39:19,565 --> 00:39:24,570
Like this guy, Jang Tae-ha was a trophy
I was rather proud of.

561
00:39:28,866 --> 00:39:31,077
But if a trophy splashes me with water,

562
00:39:31,702 --> 00:39:32,828
I don't need it anymore.

563
00:39:42,963 --> 00:39:44,130
Chairman, wait.

564
00:39:44,131 --> 00:39:45,383
Sir!

565
00:40:05,027 --> 00:40:05,861
Sir.

566
00:40:07,321 --> 00:40:08,322
Sir?

567
00:40:42,857 --> 00:40:43,774
Jang Tae-ha.

568
00:40:45,359 --> 00:40:46,277
Find him.

569
00:40:47,194 --> 00:40:48,028
Yes, sir.

570
00:40:55,703 --> 00:40:57,788
Easy. Careful.

571
00:41:00,458 --> 00:41:02,126
Let go.

572
00:41:03,294 --> 00:41:04,336
I thought…

573
00:41:05,171 --> 00:41:08,882
You said you were meeting the ladies.
Why did you drink alone?

574
00:41:08,883 --> 00:41:11,677
And you should have called me
if you were drunk.

575
00:41:19,310 --> 00:41:20,144
Why?

576
00:41:20,978 --> 00:41:22,897
Because I'm your boyfriend…

577
00:41:23,397 --> 00:41:24,398
Liar.

578
00:41:26,275 --> 00:41:28,027
I know everything now.

579
00:41:30,529 --> 00:41:31,655
Know what?

580
00:41:36,368 --> 00:41:37,578
You see,

581
00:41:38,579 --> 00:41:40,581
I found out about everything.

582
00:41:42,333 --> 00:41:43,626
What do you…

583
00:41:54,970 --> 00:41:55,888
You don't mean…

584
00:41:57,932 --> 00:41:58,766
Yeah.

585
00:42:00,851 --> 00:42:06,606
What kind of person Jang Tae-ha really is.

586
00:42:06,607 --> 00:42:08,526
I know everything now.

587
00:42:12,613 --> 00:42:13,781
So

588
00:42:14,865 --> 00:42:17,326
you don't have to pretend
to like me anymore.

589
00:42:22,122 --> 00:42:22,957
Go Eun-sae.

590
00:42:26,252 --> 00:42:27,127
Your memory.

591
00:42:29,213 --> 00:42:30,339
Is it back?

592
00:42:36,053 --> 00:42:39,014
Even if I'd lost my memory,

593
00:42:39,598 --> 00:42:43,394
how could you lie to me
about something like that?

594
00:42:47,690 --> 00:42:50,109
You shouldn't have done that to me.

595
00:43:28,063 --> 00:43:30,440
HONG'S BOXING GYM

596
00:43:30,441 --> 00:43:31,984
Hey, Tae-ha.

597
00:43:32,484 --> 00:43:33,569
She says it's back.

598
00:43:35,279 --> 00:43:36,572
Go Eun-sae's memory.

599
00:43:37,156 --> 00:43:39,742
She says she's got it all back.

600
00:43:49,043 --> 00:43:52,212
It's a relief that her memory came back
before we could get her out of here.

601
00:43:56,800 --> 00:44:00,971
Maybe she drank
because she was so shocked.

602
00:44:08,395 --> 00:44:11,397
Well, now that she remembers everything,

603
00:44:11,398 --> 00:44:14,109
she'll know she has to leave Korea
in order to survive.

604
00:44:15,319 --> 00:44:18,238
All that's left
is for her to leave safely.

605
00:44:27,998 --> 00:44:29,375
Are you okay?

606
00:44:35,422 --> 00:44:37,466
Now that her memory's back,

607
00:44:38,300 --> 00:44:39,927
this whole act is over.

608
00:44:40,511 --> 00:44:43,055
Pretending to be her boyfriend,
being all close…

609
00:44:43,972 --> 00:44:45,683
That all stops tomorrow.

610
00:44:49,311 --> 00:44:50,437
Well,

611
00:44:52,106 --> 00:44:54,024
I was never her real boyfriend anyway.

612
00:44:54,983 --> 00:44:57,653
That doesn't mean
your feelings were fake too.

613
00:45:06,370 --> 00:45:10,833
It meant I could keep her safe by my side.
That's all that matters.

614
00:45:15,170 --> 00:45:16,255
Look.

615
00:45:17,256 --> 00:45:19,465
Since things have come to this,

616
00:45:19,466 --> 00:45:22,803
why don't you just go to Japan
with Prosecutor Go?

617
00:45:24,221 --> 00:45:28,434
Just go, turn a blind eye to everything,
and spend the rest of your lives together.

618
00:45:35,190 --> 00:45:36,984
How could I leave Grandma behind?

619
00:45:39,903 --> 00:45:41,905
I'm well aware of that too.

620
00:45:43,323 --> 00:45:45,116
But for once in your life,

621
00:45:45,117 --> 00:45:47,828
you should be allowed to be selfish
and do what you want.

622
00:45:51,957 --> 00:45:52,958
I'm fine.

623
00:45:55,294 --> 00:45:57,503
Once she's smuggled out,
it's really goodbye.

624
00:45:57,504 --> 00:46:00,173
I say this because once she's gone,
that'll really be it.

625
00:46:00,174 --> 00:46:02,885
I told you, I'm fine.

626
00:46:13,020 --> 00:46:14,605
I'm really okay.

627
00:46:19,401 --> 00:46:20,861
Oh boy.

628
00:46:24,072 --> 00:46:25,449
<i>They cheated in this match.</i>

629
00:46:26,658 --> 00:46:29,703
It was nice meeting you,
Mr. Future Gold Medalist.

630
00:46:54,645 --> 00:46:55,562
<i>This one's for real.</i>

631
00:47:15,290 --> 00:47:16,250
Hey, hold on tight.

632
00:47:52,244 --> 00:47:54,162
This must be why I liked you.

633
00:48:59,895 --> 00:49:01,897
<i>Even if I can't do much else for you,</i>

634
00:49:02,397 --> 00:49:04,107
<i>on hard days like tonight,</i>

635
00:49:04,816 --> 00:49:07,778
I thought I could at least shield you
from the rain.

636
00:49:08,362 --> 00:49:10,197
I really wanted to do that for you.

637
00:49:15,035 --> 00:49:18,997
Are you thinking of marrying that girl?

638
00:49:19,581 --> 00:49:23,001
I know you like her a lot.

639
00:49:26,129 --> 00:49:29,633
She has to leave soon.

640
00:49:32,636 --> 00:49:34,387
That's the only way she can live.

641
00:49:34,388 --> 00:49:35,931
What are you talking about?

642
00:49:36,515 --> 00:49:38,850
Where would she go without you?

643
00:49:40,686 --> 00:49:42,521
I can't explain everything,

644
00:49:43,188 --> 00:49:45,190
but she has to go.

645
00:50:21,893 --> 00:50:23,562
OUR STICKY LOVE

646
00:51:10,192 --> 00:51:14,154
Subtitle translation by: Jimin Choi
